  "notes": [
    "Symbolic inline assembly preserves the generated-code entry register ABI: EDI contains low32 guest SP; ESI contains cycle budget. This is a boundary implementation, not embedded target host code.",
    "Host access violation handler retains observed uninitialized-value paths.",
    "MultiplyUnsigned64 retains the observed low-left by high-left cross product.",
    "Both multiply helpers preserve original inline assembly: signed helper has nested EBP/EDI/ESI saves inside compiler prologue; unsigned helper uses explicit carry updates of HI/LO.",
    "ROMAlternateBase 0x13FCB4D0 is the observed guest-ROM word-reader/compiler mirror offset, also used in ReadPhysicalWord and WritePhysicalWord. It is not a host address.",
    "The resolved VC7 /O2 /ML /GL /Ob1 fixture validates 16 full function bodies after relocation normalization. Raw byte exactness remains pending, and unresolved or unverified operand identities are reported separately.",
    "ResetCPU retains a remaining MMIO-clear scheduling discrepancy. CPUHostException retains register-allocation and expression-shape discrepancies.",
    "WritePhysicalByte and WritePhysicalHalf retain narrow formals. Implicit conversion of ContextRegister DWORD values reproduces the original full-DWORD pushes; explicit casts changed caller code generation.",
    "RunCPU action bits 0x1000 and 0x2000 call SaveState and LoadState(false), respectively, matching the interpreter and original call targets.",
    "RunCPU uses the evidenced local optimization-off setting and symbolic generated-code dispatcher. Its original frame contains32 unreferenced bytes after all used locals and before compiler temporaries. A nested uninitialized byte array models that measured storage; original source-level type, count, name and purpose remain unknown. Changing inferred buffer capacities moved already-correct used-local offsets and was rejected.",
    "RunCPU exact body-plus-table extent is4503bytes; the previous4504 included one alignment byte. Its emitted block to StartCPUThread is4512bytes, including9 CC bytes. StartCPUThread is30bytes followed by2 NOP bytes before0x00416A00.",
    "CPUHostException uses separate 60-byte diagnostic buffers in the early exception and invalid-index branches, an explicit valid-index else, and a POD breakpoint assignment loop. These reproduce every instruction through the opcode dispatch; opcode decoding still has CSE/register-allocation differences. Explicit memcpy emitted a redundant byte tail absent from the original; the typed assignment loop emits the observed word copy naturally.",
    "Relocation target comparisons are performed only when instruction layouts align. The two remaining instruction mismatches leave 299 target fields not compared; these fields are separate from unresolved or unverified targets in matching functions.",
    "The two nonmatching candidate extents are independently measured and pinned to the validated image: CPUHostException is 1782 bytes versus 1802 original bytes; ResetCPU is 1611 versus 1610. Their full-extent normalized difference counts are 496 and 320; earlier original-sized-prefix counts were 495 and 319.",
    "An outer switch on ExceptionCode, with the access-violation case before the general-exception default, restores the original order of all four diagnostic literals. A full .text comparison against the prior candidate changes only 19 literal PUSH operands, each retaining the same string contents; every other code byte is unchanged. This supports the source structure independently of the unresolved opcode-dispatch shape."
